{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"peewee-albite-tegus","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context / Problem\nprobe-rebar.sh accumulated stale assertions (08ce: 3 stale asserts against removed flags/keysets). Its missing 'set -e' is DELIBERATE harness design (continue past failures, report all) — a naive port or hardening pass would break it.\n\n## Approach\nPort to a Python probe harness preserving the continue-on-failure design (collect results, report all, exit non-zero if any failed — the same contract, now explicit). Assertion-parity review required: every current assertion enumerated and carried over or retired with a reason (the 08ce class came from silent drift). Do NOT add set -e semantics.\n\n## Scope\n- scripts/probe-rebar.sh -> Python equivalent\n- assertion inventory table in the change description\n\n## Testing\nSelf-test: inject one failing probe -> harness continues, reports it, exits non-zero. Parity: run both harnesses against the same build, identical pass/fail verdict per assertion.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Python harness replaces the shell probe with continue-on-failure preserved.\n- [ ] Assertion-parity table: every shell assertion mapped to ported/retired-with-reason.\n- [ ] Side-by-side run shows identical verdicts before shell deletion.","id":"f1eb-5b53-f8bd-4f2b","parent_id":"2f4c-7e5c-e782-4e97","priority":2,"tags":["shell-migration"],"ticket_type":"task","title":"Shell-to-Python Tier 2: probe-rebar.sh with assertion-parity review"},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1785640127838320001,"uuid":"89218e36-e642-4ce8-99d8-f14cac17ff58"}